  "T105: each story prop's model, made with Hyper3D Rodin from T97's model_view.png, and how props.json fits it.",
  "bounds_cm: the imported static mesh's local bounds (min, max). Rodin's front faces +Y once imported (the FBX import mirrors Y), so yaw 90 turns it to the house, as with Meshy's models.",
  "scale = size_cm / the longest side; z = -min_z * scale (the bottom on the actor's origin); grip_z = -half the height * scale (the hand holds the middle).",
  "Docs/tasks/T105.md has the findings; each prop's folder holds model.fbx, model_log.json (generation ids, prompt, fixes) and the thumbnails."
